WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.520
Devil Facial Tumour Disease is one of the
most unique

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.790
and unusual diseases in the world
because it is a transmissible cancer,

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.300
and to our knowledge there are only two
cases, in biology

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.259
of these transmissible cancers, one is in the dogs and the other one is in the devils.

00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:19.100
Canine Transmissible Venereal Tumour, as its name suggests,

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.900
is a sexually transmitted cancer and it leads to the appearance of tumours

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.800
on the external genitalia of both male and
female dogs.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.800
Both the Canine Transmissible Venereal Tumour and the Tasmanian Devil Facial Tumour Disease

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.000
are transmissible cancers spread by the transfer of living cancer cells.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.900
The canine tumour is very treatable, it's actually very responsive

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.600
to certain types of chemotherapy treatment

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:51.100
and actually almost all cases can be
cured within a few weeks through this course of chemotherapy.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.600
We're very interested in understanding why it is that chemotherapy is so successful

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.900
with treating the canine cancer, whereas
it's been tried

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.000
with the Tasmanian devil cancer and it's not
very successful at all.

